result: {"bytes":167702,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Pullum on Strunk & White's Passive Voice Advice

Pullum criticizes S&W for giving advice about passive voice while being "grammatically clueless" about identifying it. He points out that of four examples meant to demonstrate passive construction problems, three are misdiagnosed—they aren't actually passive voice.

However, S&W themselves frequently violate their own guidance. The section opening states they advocate for "a transitive in the active voice," yet the authors use passive constructions throughout their own writing, including in the very passage presenting this advice. This hypocrisy undermines their credibility on the matter.","durationMs":2839,"url":"https://languagelog.ldc.upenn.edu/nll/?p=1318"}

